---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const b='/equipment/01-03/',p7='https://psref.lenovo.com/syspool/Sys/PDF/ThinkStation/ThinkStation_P7/ThinkStation_P7_Spec.pdf',rtx='https://www.nvidia.com/content/dam/en-zz/Solutions/design-visualization/rtx-6000/proviz-print-rtx6000-datasheet-web-2504660.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="ThinkStation P7 GPU visualization node" description="Inspect a metric single-GPU workstation and replay deterministic volume-memory allocation." wide={true}><article class="equipment" id="p7"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/01-03/">← Equipment 01-03</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#p7-evidence">Evidence</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">01-03 / VISUALIZATION SYSTEMS</p><h2>Two volumes fit separately. Can they fit together?</h2><p class="eq-lede">Step through two inert volume jobs on one RTX 6000 Ada. At full resolution the second waits for the first to release memory. Reset and switch to the overview preset to see both become resident at once.</p></header>
<div class="p-cols"><section><h3>Lenovo ThinkStation P7</h3><canvas id="p7-model" aria-label="Orbitable P7 workstation with removable access panel and visible RTX 6000 Ada card"></canvas><p id="p7-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="p7-front">Front / reset view</button><button id="p7-side">Side</button><button id="p7-rear">Rear ports</button><button id="p7-panel">Open side panel</button><button id="p7-gpu">Inspect GPU</button><p>Click the front power-button mesh to advance the simulated queue, or click the side panel to inspect internals. These bindings do not power or control hardware.</p></section>
<section><h3>Teaching GPU queue</h3><div class="p-form"><label>Volume preset<select id="p7-quality"><option value="full">Full resolution</option><option value="overview">Overview · half each edge</option></select></label><label>Usable budget (decimal GB)<input type="number" id="p7-limit" min="1" max="48" step=".25" value="44"/></label></div><p id="p7-current"></p><progress id="p7-usage" value="0">Memory occupied</progress><ul id="p7-jobs"></ul><button id="p7-step">Advance one event group</button><button id="p7-run">Run to completion</button><button id="p7-reset">Reset queue</button><p id="p7-status" role="status"></p><p id="p7-parts" class="p-parts"></p></section></div>
<section><h3>Allocation and volume reference</h3><div class="p-cols"><div class="p-events"><ol id="p7-events"></ol><button id="p7-export">Download queue JSON</button><p><a href={b+'example-queue.json'}>Example event trace</a>. Preserves dataset IDs, revisions, components, FIFO order, allocated bytes and declared virtual clock.</p></div><div><canvas id="p7-slice" width="350" height="215" aria-label="Small synthetic volume slice, not the allocated full data"/><p id="p7-preview"></p></div></div></section>
<section id="p7-evidence"><h3>Reference, memory model and checks</h3><p>Selected reference: a Lenovo ThinkStation P7 with one NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada, not a claim about any installed lab machine. <a href={p7+'#page=1'}>Lenovo PSREF front/rear diagrams</a>; the published envelope is 175 × 508 × 434.4 mm (W×D×H, with feet). <a href={rtx}>NVIDIA datasheet</a>: 48 GB advertised GDDR6, 266.7 × 111.76 mm dual-slot card length and height. Fans, board mounting and internal cables are visually inferred.</p><div class="p-cols"><figure><img alt="Original ThinkStation P7 frontal rendering" src={b+'station.webp'}/><figcaption>Original front geometry: ventilated grille, red trim and vertical front I/O.</figcaption></figure><figure><img alt="Original P7 interior rendering showing the GPU" src={b+'gpu.webp'}/><figcaption>Original opened side view. The documented GPU envelope anchors card scale; board and cable paths are illustrative.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>For this calculation, 1 GB means 10⁹ bytes and 4 GB of the advertised capacity is reserved by default. Count 16-bit intensity, an 8-bit label layer, a full intensity mip chain excluding the base, two intensity staging bricks up to 256³ voxels, and 12 B per 1920 × 1080 output pixel. Each waiting job holds zero simulated GPU bytes. FIFO admits the next job only if it fits, then releases memory on completion. Overview halves all grid edges before recalculating. No real volume allocation, VRAM driver overhead, throughput, latency or FPS is measured. Times are assigned teaching events.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Reference check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>4³ voxel toy</td><td>24,883,666 bytes</td><td>24,883,666 bytes exact</td></tr><tr><td>Full A + B in 44 GB</td><td>Separate fit, together exceed</td><td>28.32 + 27.10 = 55.42 GB</td></tr><tr><td>A finishes at virtual 4 s</td><td>Release A before B starts</td><td>Complete A, release A, then start B</td></tr><tr><td>Replay</td><td>Same order and allocated bytes</td><td>Deterministic; overview admits both at t=0</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={b+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={b+'p7-rtx6000.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={b+'gpu-queue.mjs'}>Pure queue and byte model</a> · <a href={b+'vr.json'}>VR bounds and asset budget</a>. No headset test claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/01-03/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#p7 .p-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.12fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#p7 section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#p7 :is(input,select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#p7 label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0;margin:.5rem 0}#p7 label :is(input,select){width:100%;min-width:0}#p7 button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#p7 button:disabled{opacity:.5}#p7 button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#p7-model{display:block;width:100%;height:330px;touch-action:none}#p7-slice{display:block;width:100%;max-width:350px;height:auto;image-rendering:pixelated}#p7 progress{width:100%}#p7 .p-parts{font-size:.85rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#p7 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#p7 figure img{width:100%}#p7 table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#p7 td,#p7 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}@media(max-width:780px){#p7 .p-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#p7-model{height:280px}}</style>
